@startuml
title Victim Selection - Before Strategy Pattern
caption Hypothetical design comparison - Not the current implementation

left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  FontColor #222222
}

class SimulationEngine <<Hypothetical Design>> {
  + recover(policyName: String, strategyName: String)
  --
  - selectByPriority(...)
  - selectByResourcesHeld(...)
  - selectByRecoveryCost(...)
}

class Process {
  - id: String
  - priority: int
}

SimulationEngine ..> Process : evaluates candidate victims

note right of SimulationEngine
  Victim-selection algorithms
  are embedded directly in
  the simulation engine.

  The engine branches on a
  policy name to choose the
  appropriate algorithm.

  Adding another selection
  policy requires modifying
  this class.
end note

note bottom of Process
  Candidate processes have
  priorities, resource holdings
  and execution progress.

  The selection algorithms
  evaluate these properties.
end note

legend bottom
  BEFORE STRATEGY PATTERN

  Conceptual design illustrating
  tightly coupled victim selection.

  The private selection methods
  shown here are hypothetical,
  not verified Java methods.

  Problem:
  Selection logic and simulation
  orchestration are combined.
endlegend

@enduml
